Agreed, and I want to add something, which I have to do second-hand 
because I also kill-file messages cross-posted to misc.misc.

I'm afraid KPD is following a strategy occasionally used here by 
top-posters: persisting in flouting social convention while arguing that 
his behavior should be considered socially appropriate.  (Though 
"arguing" may be offering too much, as most of this recent "argument" 
seems to be that anyone who disagrees suffers from mental problems.)

I say "social convention" advisedly.  Obviously cross-posting has long
been welcome, to an extent, here and elsewhere on Usenet.  But a decent
number of the long-time rgrn regulars have said more or less directly
that cross-posting every post to misc.misc is unwelcome here.  These are
people who have the respect of virtually all the regular readers, and
who have shown an ability to quickly gain the respect of newcomers.

When trying to change a convention, it is more appropriate, at first, to
follow the convention, while arguing that the convention should be
abandoned.  If that fails (and I suspect it would fail for KPD's case) 
then it might occasionally be appropriate to deliberately flout the 
convention in order to show that we are better off without it.  I would 
suggest to KPD that this particular issue is not sufficiently important 
that it is worth offending so many respected readers.  In any case, I 
suspect KPD's battle is already lost, and that soon he will be read only 
by readers of misc.misc and readers of rgrn too lazy or unable to 
killfile him.

